WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.689
Boy and Girl's superpowers, whether the creatures
mean any harm and how they affect animals

00:00:05.689 --> 00:00:09.560
are just some of the crucial details revealed
in the original Bird Box book that don't make

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:10.760
it into the movie.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:15.070
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and today
I'm explaining seven major plot points that

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:18.650
the Netflix film Bird Box changed from Josh
Malerman's novel.

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:20.820
Obviously, film and book spoilers ahead!

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:25.380
If you've seen the various Daredevil Bird
Box memes, you might have been struck by how

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:30.259
the Marvel hero's superhuman radar sense would
have helped him in the post-apocalyptic world

00:00:30.259 --> 00:00:31.479
of Bird Box.

00:00:31.479 --> 00:00:36.219
But the Bird Box novel actually explored a
similar idea in detail with Boy and Girl becoming

00:00:36.219 --> 00:00:40.140
extra-sensitive to sounds and super-skilled
at echolocation.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:44.851
In the book, Malorie ruthlessly raised the
two children to never open their eyes, and

00:00:44.851 --> 00:00:48.989
when they were babies she'd stand over the
pair and when they woke up, she would smack

00:00:48.989 --> 00:00:53.220
them with a fly swatter if they opened their
eyes or reward them with food if they kept

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:54.780
their eyes closed.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:58.130
In the movie, we often see Boy and Girl indoors
with their eyes open.

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:02.420
Although there is a very short scene where
we see Malorie teaching the kids to use stones

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:04.710
to figure out how close an object is.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:05.710
"Listen."

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:08.120
"When they're louder, you're in an open space.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:09.610
Do you hear that?"

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:12.240
"But if they're softer, something is very
close."

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:15.050
But in the books her training is much more
extensive.

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:18.950
In the book version of the river trip, Malorie
uses the children's' heightened abilities

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:22.620
to help her navigate by identifying sounds
and nearby objects.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:27.530
In fact, Boy's hearing and echolocation skills
are so sharp that he's able to detect when

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:32.420
one of the creatures is nearby and when it's
moved on; and both he and Girl can also sense

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:35.950
subtle changes in Malorie's emotional state
just from her breathing.

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:40.650
By the way, in the book, Malorie is so fearful
of the children accidentally looking at a

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:44.610
creature that there's a chapter where she
almost pours paint thinner into their eyes

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:47.660
to blind them so they can't ever be tempted
to see.

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:51.830
Now, I mentioned how in the book, Malorie
and the children encounter one of the creatures

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:53.030
while on the river.

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:57.510
It's a terrifying moment, because the three
of them have just been hit by a flock of suicidal

00:01:57.510 --> 00:02:00.950
birds and Boy has just heard that something
is right there with them.

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:05.290
The thing moves around the boat and then it
starts to slowly pull Malorie's blindfold

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:06.290
off her face.

00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:09.440
Malorie is terrified but she puts her hand
on the blindfold and tells the creature "No.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:10.890
This is mine."

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:15.170
The creature seems to let go of the blindfold
and then moves away until Boy tells her it's

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:16.500
behind them now.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:20.140
This up-close encounter, which doesn't make
it into the movie, raises the question of

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:22.770
whether the creatures deliberately mean any
harm.

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:27.670
There's no doubt in the book or the movie
that gazing upon them is lethal to most people,

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:31.810
but the novel spends more time exploring ideas
about what they really are.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:35.920
In the book After the creature lets go of
Malorie's blindfold, she remembers something

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:39.280
that Tom said which is that "Maybe they mean
us no harm.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.530
Maybe they are surprised by what they do to
us.

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:43.700
It's an overlap […] Their world and ours.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:44.870
Just an accident."

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:48.840
What Tom seems to be suggesting is that the
creatures are probably from another world,

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:53.620
maybe even another dimension and they accidentally
arrived due to some kind of cross-dimensional

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:54.620
rupture.

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:59.210
Also, book-Malorie often refers to or thinks
of the creatures as "infinity" because, as

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:03.130
Tom also said, "whatever they are, our minds
can't understand them.

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:05.100
They're like infinity, it seems.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.740
Something too complex for us to comprehend."

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:11.430
In the movie, we get various hints as to what
the filmmakers maybe thought the creatures

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:16.100
represented and they seem to suggest a more
evil, perhaps demonic-like force.

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:20.180
Charlie listed a series of malevolent spirits
and entities during his speech about what

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:22.600
he called the Endgame for humanity.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:26.270
And in the final scenes of the movie, the
monster seemed to be actively hunting Malorie

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:30.030
and the children in the forest, which is quite
different to how it left her alone in the

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:31.459
book when she ordered it to stop.

00:03:31.459 --> 00:03:36.010
Douglas is a new character created for the
movie and John Malkovich plays the abrasive

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:37.490
role really well.

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:41.410
Some of Douglas's traits are inspired from
the book character Don who, like Douglas,

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:45.930
is generally not keen on letting new people
into the house and opposes letting in both

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:47.350
Olympia and Gary.

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:52.020
However, in the books, Don later becomes friends
with Gary who tells him stories about people

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:55.500
who've opened up the blinds in their homes
and suffer no harm.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:04:00.040
The pair ends up discussing ideas such as
"the creatures can't cause harm to someone

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:02.739
who is prepared to see them".

00:04:02.739 --> 00:04:06.520
Book-Malorie is very suspicious of Gary and
snoops around his belongings discovering a

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:08.650
notebook inside his briefcase.

00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:13.070
The notebook, like Gary's drawings in the
movie, reveals his state of mind with Malorie

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:19.189
finding sentences written left to right, right
to left, top to bottom and even in spirals.

00:04:19.189 --> 00:04:23.060
She also discovers some ideas in the notebook
that betray what Gary is really up to and

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:26.370
indicate he's likely already had encounters
with the creatures.

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:30.870
For example, he writes: "To know the ceiling
of man's mind is to know the full power of

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.039
these creatures."

00:04:32.039 --> 00:04:33.219
"But how to prove it to them?

00:04:33.219 --> 00:04:34.419
How to make them believe?

00:04:34.419 --> 00:04:37.590
I will remove the drapes and unlock the doors."

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:41.879
Gary ends up getting kicked out of the house,
however, we later discover that Don secretly

00:04:41.879 --> 00:04:44.710
let him stay, hidden away in the cellar.

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:49.680
By the time Malorie and Olympia give birth,
Don is thoroughly brainwashed by Gary, and

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:54.289
Don opens up the blinds in the house, which
results in the death of everyone except Malorie.

00:04:54.289 --> 00:04:57.039
Unlike the film, Tom also dies at this point
in the novel.

00:04:57.039 --> 00:05:02.050
By contrast, in the movie, Douglas is sceptical
of Gary throughout and even attempts to shoot

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:07.030
him to protect everyone; however, he ends
up dying at Gary's hands.

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:11.180
Overall, the subplot with Gary runs for much
longer in the book and his reappearance when

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:16.750
Malorie and Olympia give birth is a huge surprise
as they'd assumed he'd left the house a while

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:17.750
ago.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:21.339
Something the book provides more detail on
is whether the creatures can also affect animals

00:05:21.339 --> 00:05:24.539
and there are some grizzly passages which
prove that yes, they can.

00:05:24.539 --> 00:05:29.009
For example, there's an especially horrific
scene where Malorie and a dog she's with encounter

00:05:29.009 --> 00:05:32.069
a creature and the poor dog kills itself.

00:05:32.069 --> 00:05:36.159
Another particularly bloody scene in the book
occurs on the river trip when a flock of birds

00:05:36.159 --> 00:05:37.449
see one of the creatures.

00:05:37.449 --> 00:05:42.330
The birds go insane, attack each other and
kill themselves which sends down a wave of

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:47.139
dead, bloodied birds onto the boat, spattering
all over Malorie and the children.

00:05:47.139 --> 00:05:50.659
Given the movie toned down some of the more
horrific elements from the novel, I can see

00:05:50.659 --> 00:05:52.631
why these animal suicides also weren't included.

00:05:52.631 --> 00:05:54.419
Birds coo when Gary arrives.

00:05:54.419 --> 00:05:57.770
Another detail the movie changes from the
original book is Malorie's decision about

00:05:57.770 --> 00:06:00.479
who should look so that they can safely navigate
the river.

00:06:00.479 --> 00:06:04.770
The film spends a good bit of time building
up to Malorie's dilemma of choosing which

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:09.590
child will take on the potentially suicidal
mission of looking when they reach the rapids.

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:13.779
It's a heart-breaking moment with some great
acting by the young actress who plays Girl.

00:06:13.779 --> 00:06:15.479
"I'll do it."

00:06:15.479 --> 00:06:19.919
Though, of course, Malorie decides against
the plan and tries to figure out a way for

00:06:19.919 --> 00:06:21.500
everyone to survive.

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:25.080
In the book, however, they don't have to travel
through any river rapids.

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:28.729
Instead, Malorie's predicament is that she
needs to look when the river splits into four

00:06:28.729 --> 00:06:33.819
channels as she has to take the second from
the right in order to make it to the sanctuary.

00:06:33.819 --> 00:06:38.300
Book-Malorie actually plans to look very quickly
herself when this moment comes, but it's just

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:42.220
as much of a dangerous moment as what happens
in the film, because it comes just as their

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:44.919
boat bumps into the creature I mentioned earlier.

00:06:44.919 --> 00:06:49.759
Although her time in the film is short, Malorie's
sister, Jessica, played by Sarah Paulson,

00:06:49.759 --> 00:06:54.249
certainly makes an impact given the rapid,
horrifying nature of her death after seeing

00:06:54.249 --> 00:06:55.590
one of the creatures.

00:06:55.590 --> 00:07:00.720
Jessica's early demise quickly isolates Malorie
and demonstrates just how high the stakes

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:01.720
are.

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:05.349
That works for the movie, however, in the
book, Malorie's sister, whose name is Shannon,

00:07:05.349 --> 00:07:08.369
survives a lot longer as the apocalypse doesn't
happen so suddenly.

00:07:08.369 --> 00:07:12.580
In fact, Malorie and her sister hunker down
at their home for several months until one

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:17.800
day the corner of a blanket covering a window
comes loose and Shannon sees one of the creatures.

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:21.789
The loss of her sister makes Malorie feel
vulnerable, so she drives to a home that's

00:07:21.789 --> 00:07:25.629
acting as a "safe house" where people are
trying to survive together.

00:07:25.629 --> 00:07:30.139
The movie understandably wants to set the
tone much more quickly, so brings on the apocalypse

00:07:30.139 --> 00:07:34.550
in a very short timeframe, and, on top of
that, rather than a place organised to take

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:39.189
people in for shelter, Greg's house is simply
a normal home that a few survivors are lucky

00:07:39.189 --> 00:07:41.860
enough to find, more or less randomly.

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:46.281
Bird Box ends on a fairly optimistic note
when Malorie, Boy and Girl arrive at the School

00:07:46.281 --> 00:07:49.659
For The Blind and discover that Dr Lapham
has also made it there.

00:07:49.659 --> 00:07:53.469
In the book, although Malorie and the children
do reach the safety of the school, the river

00:07:53.469 --> 00:07:57.379
journey has been even more harrowing than
in the movie, with Malorie getting slashed

00:07:57.379 --> 00:08:01.089
in the shoulder by a wolf and also passing
out at one point.

00:08:01.089 --> 00:08:04.919
And the book's final chapter is also much
darker and bittersweet because what Malorie

00:08:04.919 --> 00:08:08.490
discovers at the school is that some of the
residents have gouged out their own eyes so

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:10.949
they can't be tempted by the monsters.

00:08:10.949 --> 00:08:15.149
In the novel, Rick tells her that many years
earlier the school's security was much weaker

00:08:15.149 --> 00:08:19.009
and a creature managed to break into the building
resulting in many deaths.

00:08:19.009 --> 00:08:23.529
The community then decided to blind themselves
to avoid any further risk from the creatures,

00:08:23.529 --> 00:08:27.360
although since then they've improved their
security and now new arrivals no longer do

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:28.360
that.

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:31.819
By the way, the original screenplay for the
movie also had a different, but similarly

00:08:31.819 --> 00:08:36.130
horrific, alternate ending to the one we saw
in the final film, and you can tap here for

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:39.729
all the details on that plus other deleted
scenes from the movie.

00:08:39.729 --> 00:08:42.009
So, what did you think of Bird Box?

00:08:42.009 --> 00:08:45.010
And if you've read the book, how do you feel
about the way it was adapted?

